      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Adjusting the characters into different roles might give a fresh perspective to their backstories, but I'd advise against undermining their potential for believability in their respective genres. Marcus and Andre have strong backgrounds that are more organically aligned with their suggested settings. Marcus’ street connections lend themselves perfectly to crime drama scenarios, while Andre’s technical specialty might provide critical insights in a political context, but the two are not too far apart in terms of potential narrative.\n\nJulian and Claire indeed have more traditional archetypes that lean strongly into the realm of high-stakes political thrillers, due to their roles and the context of their descriptions. Marcus and Andre stepping into offices of power are convenient but might lose the grounded, gritty realism of crime drama. Julian's CEO position and Claire's government rank seem well-suited for the political intrigue of the genre. It's the \"vibe\" and organic placement of their skills and backgrounds into their story that helps ground them in reality, as well as in their chosen genre. Marcus’ and Andre’s roles in the urban crime drama and political thriller are more believable as their personal narratives to these genres align, contributing authentic voices to their stories.",
